COMMENT     VALIDATED REFSEQ: This record has undergone validation or
            preliminary review. The reference sequence was derived from
            AC166162.6.
            
            On or before Feb 21, 2007 this sequence version replaced
            NP_001001303.1, XP_001003314.1, XP_995332.1, XP_993947.1.
            
            Summary: This gene encodes a member of the
            glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase protein family. The
            encoded protein has been identified as a moonlighting protein based
            on its ability to perform mechanistically distinct functions. The
            encoded protein was originally identified as a key glycolytic
            enzyme that converts D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate (G3P) into
            3-phospho-D-glyceroyl phosphate. Subsequent studies have assigned a
            variety of additional functions to the protein including
            nitrosylation of nuclear proteins, the regulation of mRNA
            stability, and acting as a transferrin receptor on the cell surface
            of macrophage. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript
            variants. Many pseudogenes similar to this locus are found
            throughout the mouse genome. [provided by RefSeq, Jan 2014].
            
            Transcript Variant: This variant (2) differs in the 5' UTR and uses
            a downstream start codon, compared to variant 1. The encoded
            isoform (2) has a shorter N-terminus, compared to isoform 1.
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
